3. `POST /api/v1/auth/register` (no `roleCode`) → created principal has the default `VIEWER` role; JWT subject (decoded) is the `principalCode`/email, with no `role` claim present.
4. `POST /api/v1/auth/login` as `VIEWER` → `POST /api/v1/roles/create` correctly returns 403; `GET /api/v1/roles` correctly returns 200.
